.TH VERIFY\-DOWNLOAD 1 "2026-09" "security-scanner-toolbox" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
verify-download \- verify a downloaded release artifact against a pinned checksums file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B verify-download
.I ARTIFACT
.I CHECKSUMS_FILE
.I EXPECTED_CHECKSUMS_SHA256
.SH DESCRIPTION
Verifies a downloaded release artifact in two steps, both failing closed.
.PP
First the release's checksums file must match the SHA-256 pinned in the
build arguments \(em otherwise the file itself is just another unverified
download. Then the artifact must match its own line in that file.
.PP
Pinning the checksums file rather than each per-architecture binary keeps
one constant per tool while still covering every architecture.
.PP
A missing line fails the build rather than succeeding vacuously: awk exits
non-zero when the artifact has no entry, which stops sha256sum being handed
an empty stream, which busybox treats as success.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Both checks passed.
.TP
.B non-zero
Either check failed, or the artifact has no line in the
checksums file.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Verify a downloaded binary inside a Dockerfile build stage:
.PP
.RS
.B verify-download kubectl sha256sums.txt "$CHECKSUMS_SHA256"
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sha256sum (1),
.BR scan-image (1).
Project documentation:
.UR https://github.com/fabiocicerchia/security-scanner-toolbox
.UE
